From 118d44dee98f925a733dd2a576de7cba0d020453 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:17:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] novo-app: no save prompts; saved projects write to their
 file as they change

A saved project is written to its .novo file shortly after each change
and on close, so the file always matches the screen and nothing asks
"save changes?" before new, open, close or quit. An untitled project
closed with work is kept (kept-*.novo in the untitled folder) and listed
under Unsaved on the start panel; one closed untouched is deleted.
Start-up reopens whatever was open last, untitled included. The top bar
shows Saving, Saved, Not saved yet or Not saved.

